#: src/troubleshooting.md:3
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:5
msgid ""
"This guide covers common troubleshooting techniques for Zed. Sometimes "
"you'll be able to identify and resolve issues on your own using this "
"information. Other times, troubleshooting means gathering the right "
"information (logs, profiles, or reproduction steps) to help us diagnose and "
"fix the problem."
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:9
msgid ""
"**Note**: To open the command palette, use `cmd-shift-p` on macOS or `ctrl-"
"shift-p` on Windows / Linux."
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:11
msgid "Retrieve Zed and System Information"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:13
msgid ""
"When reporting issues or seeking help, it's useful to know your Zed version "
"and system specifications. You can retrieve this information using the "
"following actions from the command palette:"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:15
msgid "<code class=\"hljs\">zed: about</code>: Find your Zed version number"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:16
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">zed: copy system specs into clipboard</code>: Populate "
"your clipboard with Zed version number, operating system version, and "
"hardware specs"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:18
msgid "Zed Log"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:20
msgid ""
"Often, a good first place to look when troubleshooting any issue in Zed is "
"the Zed log, which might contain clues about what's going wrong. You can "
"review the most recent 1000 lines of the log by running the <code "
"class=\"hljs\">zed: open log</code> action from the command palette. If you "
"want to view the full file, you can reveal it in your operating system's "
"native file manager via <code class=\"hljs\">zed: reveal log in file "
"manager</code> from the command palette."
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:24
msgid ""
"You'll find the Zed log in the respective location on each operating system:"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:26
msgid "macOS: `~/Library/Logs/Zed/Zed.log`"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:27
msgid "Windows: `C:\\Users\\YOU\\AppData\\Local\\Zed\\logs\\Zed.log`"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:28
msgid "Linux: `~/.local/share/zed/logs/Zed.log` or `$XDG_DATA_HOME`"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:30
msgid ""
"**Note:** In some cases, it might be useful to monitor the log live, such as "
"when [developing a Zed extension](https://zed.dev/docs/extensions/developing-"
"extensions). Example: `tail -f ~/Library/Logs/Zed/Zed.log`"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:33
msgid ""
"The log may contain enough context to help you debug the issue yourself, or "
"you may find specific errors that are useful when filing a [GitHub issue]"
"(https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/issues/new/choose) or when talking to "
"Zed staff in our [Discord server](https://zed.dev/community-links#forums-and-"
"discussions)."
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:35
msgid "Performance Issues (Profiling)"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:37
msgid ""
"If you're running into performance issues in Zed (hitches, hangs, or general "
"unresponsiveness), having a performance profile attached to your issue will "
"help us zero in on what is getting stuck."
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:39
msgid "macOS"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:41
msgid ""
"Xcode Instruments (which comes bundled with your [Xcode](https://apps.apple."
"com/us/app/xcode/id497799835) download) is the standard tool for profiling "
"on macOS."
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:43
msgid "With Zed running, open Instruments"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:44
msgid ""
"Select `Time Profiler` as the profiling template ![Instruments template "
"picker with Time Profiler selected](https://images.zed.dev/docs/"
"troubleshooting/instruments-template-picker.webp)"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:46
msgid ""
"In the `Time Profiler` configuration, set the target to the running Zed "
"process"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:47
msgid ""
"Start recording ![Time Profiler configuration showing the target dropdown "
"and record button](https://images.zed.dev/docs/troubleshooting/instruments-"
"target-and-record.webp)"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:49
msgid "Perform the action in Zed that causes performance issues"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:50
msgid ""
"Stop recording ![A completed Time Profiler recording in Instruments](https://"
"images.zed.dev/docs/troubleshooting/instruments-recording.webp)"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:52
msgid "Save the trace file"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:53
msgid "Compress the trace file into a zip archive"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:54
msgid ""
"File a [GitHub issue](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/issues/new/"
"choose) with the trace zip attached"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:60
msgid "Startup and Workspace Issues"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:62
msgid ""
"Zed creates local SQLite databases to persist data relating to its workspace "
"and your projects. These databases store, for instance, the tabs and panes "
"you have open in a project, the scroll position of each open file, the list "
"of all projects you've opened (for the recent projects modal picker), etc. "
"You can find and explore these databases in the following locations:"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:64
msgid "macOS: `~/Library/Application Support/Zed/db`"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:65
msgid ""
"Linux and FreeBSD: `~/.local/share/zed/db` (or within `XDG_DATA_HOME` or "
"`FLATPAK_XDG_DATA_HOME`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:66
msgid "Windows: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Zed\\db`"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:68
msgid ""
"The naming convention of these databases takes on the form of `0-"
"<zed_channel>`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:70
msgid "Stable: `0-stable`"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:71
msgid "Preview: `0-preview`"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:72
msgid "Nightly: `0-nightly`"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:73
msgid "Dev: `0-dev`"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:75
msgid ""
"While rare, we've seen a few cases where workspace databases became "
"corrupted, which prevented Zed from starting. If you're experiencing startup "
"issues, you can test whether it's workspace-related by temporarily moving "
"the database from its location, then trying to start Zed again."
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:78
msgid ""
"**Note**: Moving the workspace database will cause Zed to create a fresh "
"one. Your recent projects, open tabs, etc. will be reset to \"factory\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:81
msgid ""
"If your issue persists after regenerating the database, please [file an "
"issue](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/issues/new/choose)."
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:83
msgid "Language Server Issues"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:85
msgid ""
"If you're experiencing language-server related issues, such as stale "
"diagnostics or issues jumping to definitions, restarting the language server "
"via <code class=\"hljs\">editor: restart language server</code> from the "
"command palette will often resolve the issue."
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:87
msgid "Agent Error Messages"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:89
msgid "\"Max tokens reached\""
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:91
msgid ""
"You see this error when the agent's response exceeds the model's maximum "
"token limit. This happens when:"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:93
msgid "The agent generates an extremely long response"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:94
msgid "The conversation context plus the response exceeds the model's capacity"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:95
msgid "Tool outputs are large and consume the available token budget"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:97
msgid "**To resolve this:**"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:99
msgid "Start a new thread to reduce context size"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:100
msgid "Use a model with a larger token limit in AI settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:101
msgid "Break your request into smaller, focused tasks"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:102
msgid "Clear tool outputs or previous messages using the thread controls"
msgstr ""

#: src/troubleshooting.md:104
msgid ""
"The token limit varies by model—check your model provider's documentation "
"for specific limits."
msgstr ""
